{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unequalled-curly-erin","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"Final slice of epic 87d8. Deletes the `ticket-quality` reviewer prompt, regenerates\nthe generated catalog index, and shrinks the two test rosters that enumerate packaged\nprompts by name. After this slice the string `ticket-quality` survives only in the\nthree artifact classes this epic has excluded throughout.\n\n## Ordering\n\nThis slice must land after both of its predecessors are on `main`:\n\n- Slice 8 (`d4ca-0470-d792-49df`) repoints seven test files that resolve\n  `ticket-quality` out of the catalog — `tests/unit/test_prompt_index.py`,\n  `test_prompt_library_writes.py`, `test_prompts_git_canonical.py`,\n  `test_generated_surface_markers.py`,\n  `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py`,\n  `tests/interfaces/store/test_agent_op_safeguard.py` and\n  `tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py` — onto `code-quality`. Deleting\n  the prompt before slice 8 lands fails every one of them, because each looks the\n  prompt up by id.\n- Slice 9 (`9b96-18b7-b19e-4f85`) repoints\n  `tests/unit/workflow/test_review_skeleton.py` and the workflow example it covers\n  onto `spec-alignment`. That dependency is a correctness one rather than a\n  test-enforced one: the engine batches whatever prompt ids a step lists without\n  consulting the catalog, so the shipped example would silently name a deleted\n  prompt rather than fail.\n\nThe census below is taken on the union of `origin/main`, slice 8 and slice 9. Until\nboth land, a tree-wide grep reports more paths than AC1 and AC7 name.\n\n## Context\n\nEpic 87d8 retires the single-pass review demo and its `ticket-quality` reviewer\nprompt. Slices 1-9 removed every consumer: the engine, the workflow example, the\nvariant and override tests, the framework documentation, and the seven test files\nthat used the prompt as a stand-in for a real packaged reviewer. This slice removes\nthe prompt itself.\n\nA census with `git grep -cF -e 'ticket-quality' -e 'ticket_quality' -- src tests`\non that union reports hits in exactly four paths, and those four are this slice's\nsubject:\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/ticket_quality.md` (57 lines) — the prompt.\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json` — the generated catalog. The\n  `\"ticket-quality\"` object spans lines 75-86 and is the last entry, so removing it\n  deletes 12 lines and rewrites the preceding entry's closing brace. This file is\n  generated and is never hand-edited; it is produced by\n  `python -m rebar.llm.prompting.prompts regenerate-index`.\n- `tests/unit/test_prompt_cache_split.py:32` — one element of `_MARKED_PROMPTS`, the\n  tuple of prompts carrying the cache-split marker.\n- `tests/unit/test_prompt_front_matter.py:183` — one element of the literal set in\n  `test_built_in_prompts_are_discovered`, the guard against a vacuous parametrize.\n\nThat guard's comment above it reads \"the 6 migrated reviewers must be present\" and\nbecomes \"the 5\", so the comment still describes the set below it. The catalog drops\nfrom 6 reviewers to 5: `code-quality`, `completion-verifier`, `security`,\n`spec-alignment` and `tests`.\n\nThree artifact classes stay out of scope, as in every prior slice:\n`evals/plan-review-gate/runs/*.jsonl` (frozen corpora whose stored prompts must keep\ndescribing the run that produced them), and the tracked `.test_durations` (a\npytest-split cache that ignores unknown node IDs and regenerates itself).\n`docs/release-notes.md` is historical narrative, including this epic's own entries,\nso its existing mentions stay; this slice only prepends a new entry to it.\n\n## Change\n\nFour files plus the release note. Delete `ticket_quality.md`. Regenerate `index.json`\nwith the packaged command rather than editing it. Remove the one `\"ticket-quality\",`\nline from each of the two rosters, and correct the count in the adjacent comment.\n\nBoth rosters feed a `parametrize`, so the collected node-ID set shrinks by exactly\ntwo:\n\n- `tests/unit/test_prompt_cache_split.py::test_marked_prompt_prefix_is_variable_free[ticket-quality]`\n- `tests/unit/test_prompt_front_matter.py::test_built_in_prompt_round_trips_canonically[ticket-quality-path85]`\n\nNo other node ID is renumbered. `_packaged_prompt_paths()` sorts by prompt id and\n`ticket-quality` sorts last, so no surviving `pathNN` suffix shifts. The two files\ncollect 117 node IDs before and 115 after.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo new tests. Deleting a prompt is proven by the existing suites that enumerate the\ncatalog: a missed consumer fails at resolution. The whole affected set was run with\nslice 8's substitution and this slice's four changes applied together —\n`test_prompt_cache_split.py`, `test_prompt_front_matter.py`, `test_prompt_index.py`,\n`test_prompt_library_writes.py`, `test_prompts_git_canonical.py`,\n`test_generated_surface_markers.py`, `tests/interfaces/store/test_agent_op_safeguard.py`,\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py` and `tests/unit/workflow/` — and\nreported 937 passed, 9 skipped, with no failures.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **AC1** `git grep -cF -e 'ticket-quality' -e 'ticket_quality' -- src tests\n      scripts` prints nothing and exits 1. Before this slice it prints four paths.\n- [ ] **AC2** `test -e src/rebar/llm/reviewers/ticket_quality.md` exits 1.\n- [ ] **AC3** `python -m rebar.llm.prompting.prompts regenerate-index` exits 0 and\n      leaves `git status --short src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json` empty, proving\n      the committed index is exactly what the generator produces.\n- [ ] **AC4** `python -c \"import json;print(len(json.load(open('src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json'))))\"`\n      prints `5`. Before this slice it prints `6`.\n- [ ] **AC5** `pytest tests/unit/test_prompt_cache_split.py\n      tests/unit/test_prompt_front_matter.py -q` exits 0 and its last line is\n      `115 passed`. Before this slice it is `117 passed`.\n- [ ] **AC6** Collecting those two files with `pytest ... -q --collect-only`, keeping\n      lines containing a double colon and sorting them, differs from the same\n      collection on `origin/main` by exactly the two node IDs named in Change, both\n      as deletions, with no other line changed.\n- [ ] **AC7** `git diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD` lists exactly\n      `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/ticket_quality.md`,\n      `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json`, `tests/unit/test_prompt_cache_split.py`,\n      `tests/unit/test_prompt_front_matter.py` and `docs/release-notes.md`, and no\n      other path.\n- [ ] **AC8** `ruff check src tests docs` exits 0 with no output.\n- [ ] **AC9** `git diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD -- docs/release-notes.md` shows a\n      non-zero addition count and `0` deletions.\n- [ ] **AC10** `make verify` exits 0.","id":"f7bd-e80c-3427-48de","parent_id":"87d8-8bb6-5226-4a5b","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Delete the ticket-quality reviewer prompt and its catalog entry"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793312006481724681,"uuid":"6b4df5cc-6620-4310-9546-c244080794c1"}